Article 7
(1) In providing protection for Children as referred to in Article 2 paragraph (1), paragraph (2), and paragraph (3), Electronic System Providers carry out obligations that include:
a. obtaining the consent of the Child's parent or guardian;
b. preparing a Personal Data Protection Impact Assessment;
c. configuring the settings of Products, Services, and Features that are specifically designed to be used or accessed by Children or that may be used or accessed by Children to a high privacy level by default;
d. providing complete, correct, accurate, and non-misleading information for users to understand the Products, Services, and Features;
e. carrying out digital ecosystem education and empowerment;
f. providing notification in the form of a sign or signal in the monitoring of activities or tracking of the location of Children from the Products, Services, and Features;
g. providing a choice of functions that is appropriate to the capacity and age of the Child;
h. expressly determining the party responsible for the processing of Children's Personal Data in the provision of toys or devices that enable the toys or devices to be connected to the internet;
i. ensuring that parties appointed by or working together with the Electronic System Provider comply with the provisions on the protection of Children; and
j. appointing an official or officer who carries out the Personal Data protection function.
(2) In providing protection for Children as referred to in Article 2 paragraph (1), paragraph (2), and paragraph (3), Electronic System Providers are prohibited from:
a. using or applying concealed or non-transparent methods, techniques, or practices in the development or provision of Products, Services, and Features;
b. collecting precise geolocation information of Children; and
c. profiling Children.
(3) The preparation of the Personal Data Protection Impact Assessment as referred to in paragraph (1) letter b and the appointment of an official or officer who carries out the Personal Data protection function as referred to in paragraph (1) letter j are carried out in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.
